{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/583487-mythological-creatures-that-hide","id":583487,"title":"Mythological creatures that hide","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-08T08:28:00-07:00","id":583487,"title":"Mythological creatures that hide","content":"I might be running a game in a couple of weeks, and plan for a change of pace to our normal campaigns by starting off with the Band having to deal with a monster that has built a trap-filled lair that it leads it's victims into before doing whatever with them. The players will arrive at the lair shortly before the police do, and have to make it through the traps in order to find and defeat the creature before it slaughters the police officers.<br /> <br /> The only problem is I'm not sure what creature to use. Greek/Roman, Norse, and Egyptian mythology are the safest ones to go for due to the players having a passing familiarity with them and being new to the game. I definitely to not want to use the Aes Sidhe yet, as one of my players has really weird ideas about fairies (and refuses to except that moral was the exception), and Dragons will be too obvious for the group. My current plan is to use a Medusa, but I was wondering if anybody knew of one that fit better.<br /> <br /> The setting is London, if that's of use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T08:50:25-07:00","id":583506,"title":"","content":"How about Procrustes from the Theseus Cycle of myths by way of the Mudgett Murder House from Chicago? A hotel where people go to stay and never leave... You could even set it against a major civic event that would draw a lot of travellers, like Mudgett used the 1893 Exposition in Chicago. And maybe put some appropriately hungry Greek monsters in the basement, the &quot;real&quot; guests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T12:09:15-07:00","id":583722,"title":"","content":"You could go with a renegade Dwarf, that would be great for the traps and underground theme.<br /> <br /> The <i>Huldra</i>, Hylda, Skogsr\u00e5 or Skogfru (Forest wife/woman) is a dangerous seductress who lives in the forest. The Huldra is said to lure men down into endless cavesystems, that they would not be able to find their way out from, or lure them into the forest in order to secure her freedom or sometimes to suck the life out of a man. One of her methods is to appear suddenly out of the rain and mist, friendly and enticing to the point that no man can resist her charm.<br /> <br /> A type of wight from Northern Sweden called <i>Vittra</i> lives underground, is invisible most of the time and has its own cattle. Most of the time Vittra are rather distant and do not meddle in human affairs, but are fearsome when enraged. This can be achieved by not respecting them properly, for example by neglecting to perform certain rituals (such as saying &quot;look out&quot; when putting out hot water or going to the toilet so they can move out of the way) or building your home to close to or, even worse, on top of their home, disturbing their cattle or blocking their roads. They can make your life very very miserable or even dangerous - they do whatever it takes to drive you away, even arrange accidents that will harm or even kill you. Even in modern days, people have rebuilt or moved houses in order not to block a &quot;Vittra-way&quot;, or moved from houses that are deemed a &quot;Vittra-place&quot; (Vittra st\u00e4lle) because of bad luck - although this is rather uncommon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T13:13:30-07:00","id":583790,"title":"","content":"My suggestion - what if entering is the trap? The trap-filled maze the band is going to end up into is not the lair of the monster they hunt - it is a passage to the legendary labyrinth of the Minotaur and while its legendary prisioner was killed by Theseus long ago, he left many near-immortal descendents with the previous generations of maidens given to him and they still wander between its corridors and traps, awaiting for help from outside to leave. The PCs antagonist could mislead them, intending to use them <b>to break the children of the minotaur free</b>, hoping to make them allies in the side of Titans (or whatever other crazy or self-serving cause it serves).<br /> <br /> Just a random plot hook that came to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T19:43:31-07:00","id":584080,"title":"","content":"If you want a creature with a trap-filled liar, or a liar that <i>IS</i> a trap, I would suggest looking into spider-related myths. Or you could make one from scratch, spiders are one of the few natural creatures that lay traps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T03:48:24-08:00","id":783346,"title":"","content":"So OP, how did things go? Did that dungeon-crawl Scion session ever take off?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T08:33:33-08:00","id":783457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/583487-mythological-creatures-that-hide?p=783346#post783346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So OP, how did things go? Did that dungeon-crawl Scion session ever take off?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, unfortunately the group decided to go for Mechwarrior instead. All the information has been kept though, because this summer it's finally my turn to run a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T10:56:53-08:00","id":783524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/583487-mythological-creatures-that-hide?p=783457#post783457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, unfortunately the group decided to go for Mechwarrior instead. All the information has been kept though, because this summer it's finally my turn to run a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good luck, i feel the pain of having a game suddenly interrupted when things are heating up - in fact, also hoping to start it anew this summer (because in this hemisphere it'll be summer soon enough).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T11:04:28-08:00","id":783532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/583487-mythological-creatures-that-hide?p=783524#post783524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good luck, i feel the pain of having a game suddenly interrupted when things are heating up - in fact, also hoping to start it anew this summer (because in this hemisphere it'll be summer soon enough).</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope it goes well for you, I'm personally hedging my bets and letting my players choose from a small list of systems for me to prepare this Christmas. It's unlikely to be Scion because I'm heavily considering waiting for 2e before running the game, good chance of it being a game where all the advice from here will be useful though, possibly even Demon: the Fallen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T17:58:48-08:00","id":797573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/583487-mythological-creatures-that-hide#post583487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The setting is London, if that's of use.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Werewolf... or some other Therianthrope. As a shapeshifter, the creature can hide in plain sight, plus it also has the ability to turn other humans into more of its kind.<br /> <br /> Maybe the players destroy it, only to find out the infection has been spreading for some time, and now it's a race against the clock to track down all those infected before they tear the whole city apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}